 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-006**: When a preview is admitted to the cache for the first time, the system SHALL place it in the A1in queue at the head position.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-007**: When a cache hit occurs for an entry in the A1in queue, the system SHALL promote that entry to the head of the Am queue and remove it from A1in.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-008**: When a cache hit occurs for an entry in the Am queue, the system SHALL move that entry to the head of the Am queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-009**: When eviction is needed because admitting a new entry would exceed the 12 GiB total cache limit, the system SHALL evict from the A1in tail first; only when A1in is empty SHALL it evict from the Am tail.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: The system SHALL enforce a per-queue capacity cap of 3 GiB for A1in (25% of 12 GiB) and 9 GiB for Am (75% of 12 GiB); when an admission or promotion would cause a queue to exceed its cap, the system SHALL evict from that queue's tail until the entry fits.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-011**: The system SHALL NOT demote entries from the Am queue back to the A1in queue; Am entries are only removed by eviction from the Am tail.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-012**: The cache key SHALL be a tuple of (clip_id, revision, renderer_version); all three components are immutable identifiers.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-013**: When promoting an entry from A1in to Am, the system SHALL atomically move the entry's byte count from A1in's running total to Am's running total.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-014**: When evicting an entry from either queue, the system SHALL subtract the entry's byte count from that queue's running total.
